    <DatasetSummary announceDate="2020-10-19" hostingRepository="PRIDE" title="Quantitative proteomics reveals dual effects of calcium on radicle protrusion in soybean">
        <Description>To better elucidate the mechanisms of calcium-mediated germination of soybean seed, morphological analysis was performed in seed imbibed with different concentrations of CaCl2. Based on morphological results, radicle of germinating seed imbibed with 5 and 50 mM CaCl2 was collected for proteomic analysis.</Description>
